# The source file of this conversion, pinned.
#
# convert_bsi.py reads it from sources/ (git-ignored). The Validators
# workflow downloads it from the base below, checks it against this list
# with `sha256sum -c`, runs the converter and fails if the conversion in this
# folder comes out different. The bundle and the two coverage reports are
# therefore a reproducible record: a change of the kernel, of
# oscal_conv_lib.py or of the converter that would alter them is noticed.
#
# The base is the publisher's repository at commit 39a1193 ("Update
# artifacts"), which holds the catalogue version of 2026-07-16. The
# repository has since been rearranged; the path below exists at that commit.
#
# base: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BSI-Bund/Stand-der-Technik-Bibliothek/39a1193f3d230828ea6614eb20c94a026c9f7df0/
# into: sources
# path: Anwenderkataloge/Grundschutz++/Grundschutz++-catalog.json
#
e4c66cbc76fb8b362040fa5579999789279a1587672459d0c609c0920176002d  Grundschutz++-catalog.json
